{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (NURSE): Right, in you come. Blood pressure is 118 over 74, pulse 92, sats 98 percent.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Thanks. Umm the car park had me in bits, three laps before a spot came free, and then the rain.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (NURSE): You're 30 weeks on the chart. Any pain right now?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): No pain this minute. It's the nights, that's why I'm in.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (DOCTOR): What is it then?",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): It's this creeping in the legs at night, and I'm not sleeping a wink with it. Both legs, from the knees down, like something crawling under the skin. I'm 30 weeks and I feel about ninety come bedtime.",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (DOCTOR): How long?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): About three weeks or so. Nearly every night, worse when I lie down. Walking the landing eases it, then back it comes the minute I'm down again.",
  "[SEG0009] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): She was pacing the landing till two the last few nights. I was on the couch, half asleep, no use at all.",
  "[SEG0010] person_3 (DOCTOR): Headaches?",
  "[SEG0011] person_2 (PATIENT): Oh the neighbour's dog is at it from midnight, then the bin lorry at six, and I've a parent-teacher evening Thursday I'm nowhere ready for.",
  "[SEG0012] person_3 (DOCTOR): Headaches. Yes or no.",
  "[SEG0013] person_2 (PATIENT): No. No headaches.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (DOCTOR): Any bleeding?",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (PATIENT): No bleeding, thank God. Baby's kicking away grand.",
  "[SEG0016] person_3 (DOCTOR): Ankles swollen?",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (PATIENT): The iron tablets are woeful, they make my stomach turn. I take them with orange juice like the midwife said, and even then, ugh.",
  "[SEG0018] person_3 (DOCTOR): The ankles. Swollen or not.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (PATIENT): No, not swollen.",
  "[SEG0020] person_3 (DOCTOR): Short of breath?",
  "[SEG0021] person_2 (PATIENT): No. Breathing's grand. The stairs at the school are a fright though, steep as anything.",
  "[SEG0022] person_3 (DOCTOR): Let me see the legs. No swelling, calves are soft, pulses in both feet are there.",
  "[SEG0023] person_2 (PATIENT): They're fine in the daytime, honestly. It's only once I'm in the bed. And these shoes are a size small, my own fault, I wouldn't listen in the shop.",
  "[SEG0024] person_3 (DOCTOR): Working?",
  "[SEG0025] person_2 (PATIENT): I'm a primary school teacher, hours are half eight till three, though the copies come home with me most evenings. Diet's porridge in the morning and plenty of veg and spuds, I knocked the takeaways on the head. I walk the prom, it was four evenings a week but it's only the odd evening now since the legs started. No drink since I found out I was pregnant, and I never smoked a day in my life.",
  "[SEG0026] person_3 (DOCTOR): Diabetes or pressure in the family?",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (PATIENT): My father had diabetes in his fifties, mother did not, my other sister has the pressure but no sugar, and the brother is grand, he plays five-a-side and wrecks himself.",
  "[SEG0028] person_3 (DOCTOR): Tablets. Names and doses.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (PATIENT): Folic acid, 400 micrograms, every morning, for the pregnancy. And the ferrus sulphate, 200 milligrams, once a day, the midwife started that about six weeks back when the ferritin came back low. The chemist on the main street never has the right box, so it's the one by the church.",
  "[SEG0030] person_1 (NURSE): Ferritin was 11, six weeks ago. It's there on the chart.",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (DOCTOR): Mm. We'll repeat the ferritin and do a full blood count today. Sounds like restless legs, common enough at this stage when the iron is down. Not definite till the bloods are back.",
  "[SEG0032] person_3 (DOCTOR): Keep on the folic acid and the iron. Stretch the calves before bed, a short walk if you can, and no tea or coffee after your tea.",
  "[SEG0033] person_2 (PATIENT): Will I need a scan or anything? I start imagining the worst, I do, every little thing.",
  "[SEG0034] person_3 (DOCTOR): We might do a scan of the legs if it does not settle. Not for today.",
  "[SEG0035] person_2 (PATIENT): I've the midwife next Thursday anyway, that's booked. She'll have a feel of the bump.",
  "[SEG0036] person_3 (DOCTOR): Grand. Let's see you here in two weeks.",
  "[SEG0037] person_4 (FAMILY_MEMBER): I'll get her here, she puts the rest of us first. Rubbing the calves, does that help or am I only in the way?",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (DOCTOR): It won't do any harm. Nurse will send you for the bloods on the way out.",
  "[SEG0039] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand so. I'll scribble the questions I forget, I always think of them in the car after. Thanks."
 ],
